From: OpenIPC <openipc@openipc.org>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] usb: dwc2: treat absent VBUS GPIO as optional

Some FH86xx boards power USB VBUS directly and have no controllable
power-enable GPIO. The existing sentinel already makes that configuration
a no-op, so do not report it as a warning during every boot.

Signed-off-by: OpenIPC <openipc@openipc.org>

---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
@@ -279,8 +279,8 @@ static void fh_usb_pwr_on(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	pwren_gpio = usb_get_vbus_pwren_gpio(hsotg->dev);
 
 	if (pwren_gpio == 0xFFFFFFFF) {
-		dev_warn(hsotg->dev,
-			"Can't find usb vbus pwren gpio\n");
+		dev_dbg(hsotg->dev,
+			"No controllable USB VBUS power GPIO\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
-- 
2.43.0
